1
00:00:04,649 --> 00:00:09,070
Whiskers and Luna's World. Episode seven. Rainforests!

2
00:00:16,825 --> 00:00:21,204
Rain, rain, go away. I can't nap in my sunny spot today.

3
00:00:21,404 --> 00:00:24,825
In a rainforest, Whiskers, it rains almost every day!

4
00:00:25,025 --> 00:00:26,836
A forest... made of rain?

5
00:00:27,036 --> 00:00:31,686
No, silly! A rainforest is a warm, wet forest, full of giant trees.

6
00:00:31,886 --> 00:00:33,696
Where are the rainforests, Luna?

7
00:00:33,896 --> 00:00:37,927
Look. This is the Equator, a pretend line around the middle of the Earth.

8
00:00:38,127 --> 00:00:41,417
Rainforests grow near the Equator, where it's warm all year.

9
00:00:44,523 --> 00:00:46,962
Let's go and see! Hold on to the cushion!

10
00:00:58,204 --> 00:01:00,547
Whoosh! Up into space they flew.

11
00:01:05,396 --> 00:01:09,156
Look, the Equator! The dark green patches near it are rainforests!

12
00:01:16,911 --> 00:01:20,660
The biggest rainforest of all is the Amazon, in South America!

13
00:01:24,928 --> 00:01:27,797
That's a lot of trees. And a lot of rain.

14
00:01:41,945 --> 00:01:45,088
They landed on the dark, wet forest floor.

15
00:01:45,288 --> 00:01:46,835
Why is it so dark?

16
00:01:47,035 --> 00:01:49,040
The tall trees block out the sunshine.

17
00:01:51,855 --> 00:01:55,263
Oh no, more rain! Good thing I brought an umbrella.

18
00:02:03,019 --> 00:02:04,871
Hey... the rain is warm!

19
00:02:05,071 --> 00:02:08,837
Rainforests are warm all year, and it rains almost every day.

20
00:02:11,943 --> 00:02:14,544
Hola, amigos! Welcome to the Amazon!

21
00:02:14,744 --> 00:02:16,623
Aaah! A flying banana!

22
00:02:16,823 --> 00:02:19,237
I'm not a banana! I'm Coco the toucan!

23
00:02:21,181 --> 00:02:24,616
On the forest floor live ants... and the jaguar. Shh!

24
00:02:24,816 --> 00:02:27,855
A rainforest has layers, like the floors of a building!

25
00:02:36,191 --> 00:02:39,916
This is the understorey: small trees and big leaves, in the shade.

26
00:02:48,253 --> 00:02:51,334
And this is the canopy, the leafy roof of the forest!

27
00:02:51,534 --> 00:02:54,978
Most animals live up here, with lots of sunshine and fruit.

28
00:03:01,571 --> 00:03:06,223
More kinds of plants and animals live in rainforests than anywhere else on land!

29
00:03:10,491 --> 00:03:12,728
Hey, who's that, hanging upside down?

30
00:03:15,834 --> 00:03:18,335
Hel... lo... there.

31
00:03:18,535 --> 00:03:21,328
That's Mossy the sloth. He's very, very slow.

32
00:03:21,528 --> 00:03:24,563
I... like... to hang... and nap.

33
00:03:24,763 --> 00:03:27,373
I'm a champion napper. Watch this!

34
00:03:33,966 --> 00:03:35,720
Care... ful...

35
00:03:38,535 --> 00:03:41,550
Whoa! Canopy! Understorey! Forest flooor!

36
00:03:48,433 --> 00:03:50,924
Oh. Hello, big kitty. Nice spots.

37
00:03:54,611 --> 00:03:58,016
I fell on purpose. I was visiting every layer.

38
00:03:58,216 --> 00:04:00,919
You missed one! The emergent layer, at the very top!

39
00:04:10,999 --> 00:04:14,357
The emergent trees are the tallest. Eagles live up here!

40
00:04:14,557 --> 00:04:17,453
And all these leaves help make the fresh air we breathe.

41
00:04:20,559 --> 00:04:22,451
Good... bye...

42
00:04:22,651 --> 00:04:24,952
He'll finish saying goodbye next week.

43
00:04:31,544 --> 00:04:36,936
Remember! One. Rainforests are warm and rainy, and grow near the Equator.

44
00:04:39,751 --> 00:04:43,783
Two. The Amazon is the biggest rainforest in the world.

45
00:04:46,599 --> 00:04:51,810
Three. Rainforests have layers, and most animals live high up in the canopy.

46
00:04:58,403 --> 00:05:02,756
Quiz time! Is a rainforest cold and dry, or warm and wet?

47
00:05:05,862 --> 00:05:09,141
Warm and wet! It rains almost every day.

48
00:05:11,666 --> 00:05:16,858
Do most rainforest animals live on the forest floor, or up in the canopy?

49
00:05:19,963 --> 00:05:22,485
High up in the canopy! Well done!

50
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:32,565
Back home, the rain had stopped.

51
00:05:32,765 --> 00:05:34,848
Can we visit Mossy again tomorrow?

52
00:05:35,048 --> 00:05:37,892
Sure. But first, a nap. The right way up.

53
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:46,083
Next time, the frozen poles! Goodnight, rainforest.

